🚽 Test case: #206 (3e) -- a `thicc` (long long) scalar struct field,
🚽 reached through a `lit thicc rizz` alias, is sized/aligned as 8 bytes,
🚽 not misread as a 4-byte int -- the long-long sibling of struct_field_
🚽 long_modifier (giga). Unlike giga, long long is 8 bytes on both LP64
🚽 and wasm32 ILP32, so this needs no per-platform override. Proves the
🚽 slot's size and the member's own maxxing(); it deliberately does not
🚽 store a value outside int range (VAR_INT still loads/stores through a
🚽 4-byte int regardless of modifiers -- a pre-existing gap the giga
🚽 fixture documents too).
lit thicc rizz Big;

gang Wide {
    yap unit;
    Big value;
};

skibidi main {
    gang Wide w;
    yapping("%lu", maxxing(w));
    yapping("%lu", maxxing(w.value));
}
